<title>JAPAN: TOCOM to raise Dec rubber futures margin fee.</title>
<headline>TOCOM to raise Dec rubber futures margin fee.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Commodity Exchange (TOCOM) said on Tuesday it would raise the margin requirements on its December rubber futures contract by 10,000 yen per trading lot, effective from Wednesday.</p>
<p>The total margin requirement for the spot December, which expires this Friday, will be 157,750 yen, TOCOM said in a statement.</p>
<p>The increases are intended to cool overheated trade. The requirement on other contracts, except the January, remain unchanged at 52,500 yen, it said.</p>
</text>
